# 07-memory-model.md §11.5: a `Channel(T)` parameter MUST NOT be `inout`. Phase 39:
# a `$T` in the signature used to buy an exemption -- resolve_program `continue`d
# past a generic template before this check, so tychoc ACCEPTED, compiled and RAN
# this, and Phase 32 mirrored the gap in tychoc0 so the two agreed. The three
# declaration rules now run ahead of that `continue`. Both compilers reject
# (differential); the concrete form is tests/reject/chan_inout_param.ty.
fn f(c: inout Channel(int), p: $T) -> int:
    return 1

fn main():
    ch := channel(int, 2)
    println(str(f(&ch, 5)))
